      "writtenOn": "2025-03-31T21:57:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should exercise the following:\n\n1) Renaming the secret in the job.  ie:\n\n```\n- job:\n    secrets:\n      - secret: project2-oidc-secret0\n        name: login_secret\n```  \n\nNote that I intentionally named the secret with hyphens since that\u0027s not allowed in Ansible, but when we rename it to login_secret, that will be what Ansible sees.  We should test that login_secret overrides a job variable with the same name.  This is worth exercising because we have new variable merging code for the OIDC secrets.\n\n2) Return secret vars precedence:\n\nUse zuul_return to return a secret variable with the same name as a secret (eg, \"login_secret\" in the above example), and ensure that the job sees the oidc secret, not the returned value (real secrets have precedence over returned secret data).\n\n3) Pass-to-parent:\n```\n- job:\n    name: child-job\n    parent: parent-job\n    secrets:\n      - secret: something\n        pass-to-parent: true\n```\n\nThat should make the secret available in all of the playbooks of the parent job, so we will need to validate the behavior in a playbook that runs from the parent job, not the child job.",
      "revId": "17080a304df5de0be42318cf21d77ae45108862c",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
